cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this screening pipeline or its candidate list, please cite it as below."
title: "dsDNA candidate screening for IQS binding"
abstract: >-
  A four-stage in-silico screening pipeline that reduces 10,000 randomly
  generated DNA sequences to a shortlist of 20 double-stranded candidates for
  binding IQS (2-(2-hydroxyphenyl)-thiazole-4-carbaldehyde), a quorum-sensing
  signal molecule of Pseudomonas aeruginosa, intended for a dsDNA-based
  electrochemical sensor. Combines sequence filtering, heuristic scoring,
  nearest-neighbour duplex thermodynamics and AutoDock Vina docking.
